WEBVTT

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:03.980
Days gone by,

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:03.980
in which there is liquor

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:16.680
Hey.

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:19.690
Yeah.

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:23.510
You're both pretty late.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:25.560
Have a seat.

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:30.560
Is it just me, or is something different?

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:32.510
Episode 28

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:32.510
The Dark Era

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.210
You seem rather relaxed.

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:33.370
Do I?

00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:38.280
Believe it or not, 
I'm more important than either of you.

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:40.010
<b>Dazai Osamu</b>

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:40.010
<b>Youngest Port 
Mafia Executive</b>

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:40.010
You'd better respect me lots.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:42.520
<b>Sakaguchi Ango</b>

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:42.520
<b>Port Mafia Informant</b>

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.530
Hear that, Odasaku-san?

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:43.850
No kidding.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:45.270
<b>Oda Sakunosuke</b>

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:45.270
<b>Low-level Port Mafia Agent</b>

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:45.260
We aren't worthy.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:48.270
Why don't we lowly grunts drink together?

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:48.670
Yes.

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:49.790
We don't have a choice, do we?

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:52.850
I want to toast, too.

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:55.040
You're all right today.

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:55.950
All right how?

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:57.090
You don't smell.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.020
The first time I met you two...

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:00.740
You were stinky and nasty.

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:02.750
You made my office smell.

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:05.660
That was the nature of our work that day.

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:11.410
You say that, but would you be happy if we were all shiny and smelled like flowers?

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:13.050
No, please! That's creepy.

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:16.930
Anyway, cheers.

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:21.540
Maintenance?

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:24.300
Oh, yes.

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:26.810
It's a precious tool of my trade.

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:29.220
I just remembered that 
there used to be a superstition

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:32.350
about your soul getting sucked out 
every time a picture's taken of you.

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:34.310
Your soul gets sucked out, huh?

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:36.580
Ango! Take lots of pictures of me!

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:38.670
Until my life runs out! Please!

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:40.080
That would be a waste of film, so no.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:41.070
Gimme for a second.

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:41.310
Wait—

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:42.840
Odasaku, say cheese!

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:48.580
You can develop film?

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:51.950
You move a lot whenever I click, don't you?

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:52.750
Do I?

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:56.850
And then, like, stuff happened and stuff.

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:57.830
Sure, sure.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:01:59.650
<i>I think I'm drunk.</i>

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:01.460
That's when I had this curi—

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:04.380
curious thought, that I could die.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:05.500
Rats.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:06.960
What do you mean, rats?

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:09.980
I think Odasaku-san thought 
you were talking about curry.

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:10.970
Curry, huh?

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:12.590
Maybe I'll make some.

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:14.260
I'm a good cook.

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:15.450
Lies.

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:18.270
Your cooking needs to be censored.

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:21.280
It might be fun to cook together, 
the three of us.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:24.020
We'll bring one item each 
and put it in the pot.

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:26.030
That's what they call "dark hot pot"!

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.500
Come on, Ango, stop being so cranky.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:30.590
Look at Odasaku.

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:32.220
Right, Odasaku?

00:02:32.570 --> 00:02:34.480
Dazai, your finger's touching me.

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:36.540
<i>I have so much to say.</i>

00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:39.540
Hot pot sounds like a good idea
 at this time of year.

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:42.790
I know! Since you guys are so 
busy with your duties...

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:45.600
I'll make you some special 
superhuman stamina hot pot!

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.050
This can only end badly.

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:48.720
It'll be especially good this time!

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:51.320
It's going to taste of miracles
 like you've never known.

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:53.820
I should probably ask. What's in it?

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:56.760
The remains of superhuman stamina hot pot that I accidentally burnt,

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:59.740
fermented just a little bit 
with vinegar and Tabasco,

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:01.930
wrapped and concealed 
in kindness and love.

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:03.210
That's not concealed!

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:05.330
How could that possibly be any good?!

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:06.840
Cooking is love.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:08.620
You trust love way too much.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:11.220
Say something, Odasaku-san!

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:12.810
It wouldn't be good?

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:15.830
What part of what he just said 
gives you that confidence?

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:17.920
What part? I mean...

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:20.350
Dazai said it would be good.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:22.100
That's all.

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:23.010
Uh-huh...

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:25.590
Exactly. It's <i>really</i> good, Ango.

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:27.980
It's eye-meltingly, cheek-poppingly good.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:29.110
You've got that mixed up.

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:33.240
We'd love to try it someday, Dazai.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:34.480
Of course.

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:49.870
Who's writing New Year's cards?

00:03:50.050 --> 00:03:50.860
Me.

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:53.750
Listen, Dazai-kun...

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:56.990
New Year's greeting cards are
 intended to express gratitude

00:03:56.990 --> 00:04:01.850
for the passing year and a wish for 
ongoing friendship in the coming year.

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:03.740
Do you have that in you?

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:05.100
Sure I do. How rude.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:08.770
Anyway, I grab a brush and some
 New Year's greeting cards,

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:10.390
and doodle a little something...

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:11.710
Whoops, I messed up.

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:14.900
<b>Happy 
New Ye</b>

00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:13.600
I ran out of space.

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:14.880
Rookie handwriting mistakes!

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:16.620
Whatever, I'll send this one to the boss.

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:17.890
What about your gratitude?!

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:20.150
Maybe I should have more than just text.

00:04:20.390 --> 00:04:21.730
Like drawings?

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:23.230
The zodiac would be the thing to do.

00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:23.910
The zodiac, huh?

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:25.700
Next year is the year of the ox.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:28.640
This looks like a cow, right?

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:31.580
Please don't waste a card 
on a draft, Odasaku-san.

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:32.320
Done.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:34.920
How are you so good?!

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:38.100
The kids nag me to draw for them.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.360
Still, though...

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:40.790
Cool, I'll draw something, too.

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:41.840
Done!

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:42.540
Creepy!

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:45.330
It looks like a ghost
 haunting Odasaku's cow.

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:45.990
That's so rude.

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:47.670
They're Holstein buddies.

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:50.180
It looks like it's being attacked by demons!

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:52.160
So, what should I do with the next one?

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:53.550
Are you done yet?

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:55.830
Why don't you just make a sweet potato stamp?

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:56.550
What's that?

00:04:56.550 --> 00:04:58.360
You carve a stamp out of a sweet potato.

00:04:58.360 --> 00:04:59.770
That sounds fun!

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:00.720
Sir!

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:02.950
You have sweet potatoes?

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:15.960
<b>r6aY waN
 yqq6H</b>

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:15.960
<b>aʞusonuʞ6S
 ebO</b>

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:11.690
Impressive!

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:13.740
But you're making rookie stamp mistakes.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.960
<b>Rookie stamp mistakes</b>

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.960
<b>Text is backwards
 if you carve it
 into a stamp 
as normal</b>

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:18.990
Meanwhile, I was careful about that.

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:20.130
My text is perfect.

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:23.960
<b>Curse</b>

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:21.080
Happy Year of the Ox!

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:22.120
You wrote "curse" instead!

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:23.280
Also, is this even a cow?

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:25.290
Messed up again.

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:27.630
That's yet another card 
for me to give the boss.

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:29.810
Are you going to send 
all your cards to the boss?

00:05:29.810 --> 00:05:32.330
What about your cards, then, Ango?

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:33.470
No.

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:34.620
I don't want to show you.

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:35.830
Hey, Odasaku! Take!

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:36.470
Woof.

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:38.970
Good boy. Good boy.

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:40.980
It's even lamer than I thought.

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:43.210
That's why I said no!

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:44.240
Sorry.

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:46.400
Let's make it a collab with my potato stamp.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:47.840
My poor cow.

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:51.830
Stop enjoying this
 and stop him, Odasaku-san!

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.860
I'm not enjoying this.

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:54.820
Forget it.

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:56.090
These are your greeting cards, Dazai-san.

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:57.630
If you're happy with them, whatever.

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:02.000
Done.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:04.220
The last shenanigans of the year.

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:08.440
Imagine what it must be like to receive
 those cards first thing in the new year.

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:09.380
Well, then...

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:15.020
<b>Oda 
Sakunosuke-sama</b>

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:15.020
<b>Sakaguchi
 Ango-sama</b>

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:13.230
I don't know if we'll see each other in the new year, so I'll give these to you now.

00:06:15.010 --> 00:06:17.230
Happy early new year!

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:25.030
<b>Yay! Happy
 New Year</b>

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:25.030
<b>Happy 
New Year</b>

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:24.410
It's kind of sobering when your own 
shenanigans come back at you, huh?

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:25.030
Yeah.

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:28.300
It comes with a cash gift, though, 
so maybe it's worth something.

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:29.360
Thanks, Dazai.

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:30.800
You're so positive.

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:31.580
Of course I am.

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:33.610
I have a happy personality.

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:36.650
They're intended to express 
gratitude for the passing year

00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:38.540
and a wish for ongoing friendship in the coming year.

00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:41.820
<i>Gratitude and ongoing friendship...</i>

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:44.760
Ango.

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:47.170
Let's be good to each other.

00:06:49.150 --> 00:06:51.990
Okay, let's toast to the new year!

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:53.920
It's still early for that.

00:06:58.030 --> 00:06:59.310
Dazai-kun, what are these?!

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:01.050
Are they cursed? Creepy!

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:07.430
What are you reading, Odasaku?

00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:12.270
"One day, a man was walking 
alone in a forest when..."

00:07:12.270 --> 00:07:14.300
I'm asking about the title.

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:15.540
"That's when..."

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:16.360
Horror, huh?

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:18.290
"What appeared before him?"

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:24.380
<b>What appeared before him?</b>

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:19.860
"1. A white rabbit"

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:24.380
<b>1. A white rabbit</b>

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:21.380
"2. A large wolf"

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:24.380
<b>2. A large wolf</b>

00:07:21.380 --> 00:07:22.880
"3. Candlelight"

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:24.380
<b>3. Candlelight</b>

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:24.370
It's a psychological test?!

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:27.350
If I had to choose, I guess 1.

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:28.870
I'll go with 3, then.

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:35.680
If you chose 1, you seek the purity of white and the warmth of the rabbit.

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:37.760
You are, in fact, prone to loneliness.

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:39.900
No way.

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:44.310
If you chose 2, you seek the strength of a wolf.

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:46.390
Deep down, you are prone to loneliness.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:50.310
If you chose 3, seriously,
 you're <i>really</i> prone to loneliness.

00:07:50.310 --> 00:07:51.640
Wait, mine was so half-hearted!

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:54.400
I don't think you should trust that book.

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:55.010
You think so?

00:07:55.010 --> 00:07:57.530
Why don't we try one more question, then?

00:07:57.530 --> 00:07:59.280
Please, Ango?

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:00.680
No.

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:02.310
Here goes, then.

00:08:03.090 --> 00:08:08.010
"You are in paradise. 
You can have anything you'd like."

00:08:08.010 --> 00:08:11.070
"What is the first thing that comes to mind?"

00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:11.480
Curry, curry, curry...

00:08:11.480 --> 00:08:12.200
Curry.

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:15.660
Of course I'm going to think about curry
 if you keep whispering "curry" in my ear!

00:08:16.210 --> 00:08:19.780
Apparently, it's the first impression you give off to the person of your dreams.

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:21.030
I guess it works?

00:08:21.030 --> 00:08:22.240
This is a misunderstanding!

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:23.890
I like curry, too.

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:26.080
Please don't try to make sense of it!

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:27.340
Sorry.

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:30.320
I'll make it up to you by doing
 a psychological test for you two.

00:08:30.790 --> 00:08:34.320
One day, when I was visiting Ango's work room,

00:08:34.730 --> 00:08:36.560
I found a book that caught my attention, and...

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:44.750
I put the book back and left.

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:46.610
That actually happened, didn't it?

00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:48.450
Wait! There's more.

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:52.080
I, Dazai Osamu, have been
 regretting it ever since.

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:53.590
Now, here's the question:

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:58.100
If I were to apologize with sincerity now,
 would Ango forgive me?

00:08:58.100 --> 00:08:59.970
I knew it! It actually happened!

00:08:58.470 --> 00:08:59.970
There, there.

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:01.580
He would.

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:02.440
Odasaku's correct.

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:03.340
Wait, why?!

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:07.080
Man, I feel better 
thanks to that psychological test.

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:08.970
That's not a psychological test.

00:09:10.470 --> 00:09:12.230
Here's one last question.

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:15.870
"There are stars in the night sky. 
How many do you see?"

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:18.780
The answer is easy.

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:20.060
There are zero.

00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:21.420
It's pitch dark.

00:09:23.570 --> 00:09:24.700
Uh, well...

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:28.110
I think I would want <i>something</i>, 
even if it's just a candlelight.

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:30.160
You <i>are</i> prone to loneliness, Ango.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:33.020
Odasaku, what's this test about?

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:36.760
<b>This test reveals your
 level of friendship!</b>

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:36.760
<b>You'll have as many good times
 with your friends as you
 said you saw stars.</b>

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:40.470
I mean, it's just a test.

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:42.710
The three of us just 
happened to gather here.

00:09:42.710 --> 00:09:44.480
It's nothing more.

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:47.700
We don't even know if we're 
going to be safe tomorrow.

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:48.710
That's true.

00:09:48.710 --> 00:09:50.650
I didn't get to die today, again.

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:54.840
Another ordinary day is coming
 to an end. That's all.

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:56.770
I like that, Odasaku.

00:09:58.530 --> 00:10:01.730
Well, then, a toast to an ordinary 
day for the three of us.

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:03.820
Cheers.
